      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand why `fIsBottomUp` affects only `dstRow` but not `srcRow`.\n\nAssumption: I assume that the `image::docecs::BmpDecoder` handles top-down-vs-bottom-up internally (because I assume that [`image::ImageDecoder::read_image`](https://docs.rs/image/latest/image/trait.ImageDecoder.html#tymethod.read_image) always reads the pixel the right-side-up).\n\nIf the assumption above is true, then I think that `fIsBottomUp` should affect both `dstRow` and `srcRow`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 328,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "7ba49709a2ebb814355ec5b1518b1cb42c6fb834",
