      "writtenOn": "2026-02-09T22:36:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch, the bottom up handling was in a mixed-inconsistent state. I have refactored it to make it consistent and encapsulated on the rust code, so from C++ there is no need to know if it is bottom up or top down. Mainly:\n- BMPDecoder in image crate will be reversing rows to adjust to be top down orientation. This means that a fully decoded image will be already top down orientation. When partial decoding, then rows_decoded will return the number of rows and the orientation\n- FFI will return the full image when fully decoded or the trimmed rows. There will be an auxiliary method returning the start row and the number of rows of the decoded image (so if it is top down it will be from 0 to n - 1; if it is bottom up it will be from height - n to height - 1)\n- SkBmpRustCodec will just copy the range of rows to the given position, or the full image if it is fully decoded.\n\nWith this, only BMPDecoder is keeping internally the top_down boolean; the FFI will get it as required on responses to rows_decoded but it will not store it internally, and SkBmpRustCodec will not have knowledge about top_down boolean.",
      "parentUuid": "978ba4ad_184a18d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 328,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "7ba49709a2ebb814355ec5b1518b1cb42c6fb834",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29f92a19_c0ba1432",
