      "writtenOn": "2026-02-05T23:52:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here I also don\u0027t understand why `fIsBottomUp` affects only `dstRow` but not `srcRow`.  When `fIsBottomUp` is true and `kIncompleteInput` happens, then I expect that the *last* rows of `srcImage` are populated and can be copied to the *last* rows of `dstImage`.  (And the code in this case seems to copy the *first* [not-populated-yet?] rows of `srcImage` to the *last* rows of `dstImage`.)\n\nIf this is indeed a problem, then would it be possible to add a test that covers a bottom-up image (e.g. verifying pixels in the first and last rows, and expecting them to differ).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 407,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 407,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "7ba49709a2ebb814355ec5b1518b1cb42c6fb834",
